# Tawny owl

The tawny owl is the common woodland owl of Europe and western Asia, stocky and
round-headed, with black eyes and no ear tufts. It is strictly nocturnal,
leaving its daytime roost against a trunk only once the light has gone from the
canopy. Small mammals make up most of its diet, though a town pair will take a
good many sparrows and beetles instead. Its quavering hoot and sharp kewick
contact call are the sounds most people mean when they describe a European wood
after dark. See [[strigidae]].
